  "Id": 587,
  "Title": "Annual Environment Excellence Award 2008 for Aga Khan University Hospital, Karachi",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Aga Khan University Hospital , Karachi won the Annual Environment Excellence Award 2008 at a ceremony held on Wednesday, July 2, 2008.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<p>In recognition of its contribution to sustainable development and environment-friendly practices, Aga Khan University Hospital , Karachi won the Annual Environment Excellence Award 2008 at a ceremony held on Wednesday, July 2, 2008. The award was part of a nationwide competition organised by the National Forum for Environment &amp; Health in collaboration with United Nations Environment Programme.</p><p>NFEH looked at the organisation's performance in 2007 and at criteria for the competition included: Environment, Health and Safety (EHS) management programme of the organization; leadership commitment; staff participation, goals and objectives; training programmes and progress; incident reporting and analysis; waste management and performance monitoring, measurement and improvement.</p><p>The University Hospital ensures the consistency of its high quality care through a meticulous process of continual quality assurance.</p>",
